                <pb facs="0754" n="656" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg656"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hunter to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1899-11-07"><hi rendition="#italic">November 7,
                        1899</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Hunter reports that Mr. Hay’s rights to indemnity, which he demanded in
                    accordance with instruction No. 195 of October 6, are denied by Guatemalan
                    Government, which offers to submit to an arbitral tribunal all disputed points
                    for the determination of the question as to the existence of rights to damages,
                    and if so, the amount of such damages.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
